    /// Enforce placing lifecycle hooks before test cases in the same block.
    ///
    /// Lifecycle hooks such as `beforeAll`, `beforeEach`, `afterEach`, and
    /// `afterAll` describe the setup and teardown shared by the tests in a
    /// block. When a hook appears after a test case, it becomes harder to spot
    /// how the tests are set up and torn down, because the reader has to scan
    /// past the test cases to find it. Keeping every hook above the test cases
    /// in its block makes the intent of the block clear at a glance.
    ///
    /// Each `describe` block, as well as the top level of a file, is treated as
    /// its own scope. A hook is only reported when at least one test case
    /// (`it` or `test`) appears before it in the same scope.
    ///
    /// ## Examples
    ///
    /// ### Invalid
    ///
    /// ```js,expect_diagnostic
    /// describe('foo', () => {
    ///   it('should do bar', () => {});
    ///   beforeEach(() => {});
    /// });
    /// ```
    ///
    /// ### Valid
    ///
    /// ```js
    /// describe('foo', () => {
    ///   beforeEach(() => {});
    ///   it('should do bar', () => {});
    /// });
    /// ```
    ///
    pub UseTestHooksOnTop {
        version: "next",
        name: "useTestHooksOnTop",
        language: "js",
        recommended: false,
